 ### [Noise Derivative FBM](16976-noise-derivative-fbm.md)
-A terrain generation technique that uses the analytic derivatives of value noise to modulate height accumulation in an FBM loop. It differs from standard FBM by using gradient magnitude to dampen height accumulation, and from basic Derivative FBM by explicitly returning the derivative vector for lighting and erosion calculations. [16976-noise-derivative-fbm.md]
+Noise Derivative FBM is a procedural terrain generation technique that uses analytic derivatives to modulate height accumulation in an FBM loop. It differs from standard FBM by dampening height accumulation with gradient magnitude, and from basic Derivative FBM by explicitly returning the derivative vector for lighting and erosion calculations. Choose it when generating detailed, physically plausible landscapes with flat plateaux and accentuated steep regions.
 
